{
  "slug": "cc-boost",
  "name": "Cc Boost",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "cc-boost is an open-source Claude Code plugin that reduces token consumption by filtering noisy tool output before it reaches the context\nwindow. It strips ANSI escape codes, collapses repetitive npm/pip progress bars into single summary lines, and folds consecutive node_modules  stack frames into compact summaries — typically achieving 60–90% character reduction on verbose command output. It also intercepts interactive  scaffold commands (create-next-app, vite, sveltekit, remix, angular) that Claude cannot run interactively, prompting Claude to ask the user for  configuration choices first before re-running with the correct flags.",
  "longDescription": "Installs with `claude plugin install cc-boost@claude-community` from `sworddut/cc-boost`.\n\n将 Bash 命令包装为管道，在输出到达 Claude 前进行清洗：\n\ncc-boost is an open-source Claude Code plugin that reduces token consumption by filtering noisy tool output before it reaches the context\nwindow. It strips ANSI escape codes, collapses repetitive npm/pip progress bars into single summary lines, and folds consecutive node_modules  stack frames into compact summaries — typically achieving 60–90% character reduction on verbose command output. It also intercepts interactive  scaffold commands (create-next-app, vite, sveltekit, remix, angular) that Claude cannot run interactively, prompting Claude to ask the user for  configuration choices first before re-running with the correct flags.",
